_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given statements.\n\n- Statement I is true. The rectangle $R$ covers the region $D$ completely.\n\n- Statement II is false. The integrals have not been stated correctly with respect to the domains $R$ and $D$ (they have been swapped).\n\n- Statement III is false. The rectangle $R$ does not cover the region $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"I only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407298 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407301 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407298 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "080248f8-ed70-5a9f-8bf1-a2b4de4eb4f7" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407298 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152827 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407299 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407302 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407299 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "30bd25e3-ac80-5e5b-b4e0-5224a24a94ed" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407299 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407295 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407300 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407298 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407300 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "4e94e485-56a2-5844-806a-2096ce99769f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407300 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186152826 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407301 #edb/ref 1058 #edb/ref 17592186407299 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407301 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "5f132e51-d1d4-5811-8af1-98e3b3699b32" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407301 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407297 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407302 #edb/ref 1062 #uuid "98a2aaad-910d-5774-ad63-69bb719493bb" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186407302 #edb/ref 1063 #edb/ref 17592186407296 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425932 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425933 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425934 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186425910 #edb/ref 1043 #edb/ref 17592186425935 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186