ng)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-x, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}\\,\\text{and}\\,{∬}_{D}({y}^{2}-x)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of the rectangular domain $R?$\n\nI. $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,1]$\n\nII. $R=[-1,1]\\times [-1,2]$\n\nIII. $R=[-2,2]\\times [-1,0]$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444896 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "9b739dd6-c1ea-5425-a4f3-ff629b5d83cc" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444896 #edb/ref 1074 "Notice that if $R$ covers $D$ completely and we define \n\n$$\nf(x,y)=\\{\\begin{aligned}{y}^{2}-x, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwe obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({y}^{2}-x)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given rectangles.\n\n- Rectangles I and III do not cover the region $D.$\n\n- Rectangle II covers the region $D$ completely.\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444897 #edb/ref 1068 #edb/ref 17592186444895 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444897 #edb/ref 1069 "q-80568" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444897 #edb/ref 1070 #edb/ref 17592186045487 #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444897 #edb/ref 1071 "![](images/12/12acb33aa174f1c174a538a89881dd19245f733c6b39df37f9ebbdc1f86442d5.png)\n\nConsider the region $D$ shown above. If $R=[-3,1]\\times [-1,2],$ and\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({2}^{x}-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A,\n$$\n\nwhich of the following could be the definition of $f(x,y)?$\n\nI. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x}-y, & (x,y)\\in R \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\notin R\\end{aligned}$\n\nII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x}-y, & (x,y)\\in R∖D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in D\\end{aligned}$\n\nIII. $\\{\\begin{aligned}{2}^{x}-y, & (x,y)\\in R\\cap D \\\\ 0, & (x,y)\\in R∖D\\end{aligned}$" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444897 #edb/ref 1072 #uuid "fac0df1b-f9cc-511c-8006-433930d0444f" #edb/ref 17592186045417] [17592186444897 #edb/ref 1074 "First, let's draw our region $D$ and rectangle $R:$\n\n![](images/56/56f6557f98674b0f651a781e6226ba9d207273e30136e3396c3aabcf91a64024.png)\n\nNotice that the rectangle $R$ contains the region $D$ completely. \n\nNow, if we define $f(x,y)$ to be equal ${2}^{x}-y$ on $D$ and to be equal $0$ outside $D,$ we obtain\n\n$$\n{∬}_{D}({2}^{x}-y)\\,\\text{d}A={∬}_{R}f(x,y)\\,\\text{d}A.\n$$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each of the given functions.\n\n- We cannot use functions I and II. Both of these functions are not identically zero for all points in $R∖D.$ For example, $(x,y)=(1,0)\\in R∖D$, but the functions are nonzero at this point.\n\n- Function III equals ${2}^{x}-y$ on $D$ and equals $0$ outside $D.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"III only.\"" #edb/ref 17592186045417]}
